# What the image build is allowed to see.
#
# The build context is the repository root, because deploy/Dockerfile is invoked
# with `context: ../..` from the compose files. Without this file that context is
# around 4.5 GB — android/ alone is 4.3 GB of Gradle output and emulator debris —
# and every byte of it is tarred up and handed to the daemon on every build, for
# a Dockerfile that copies four things.
#
# Size is the boring half. The half that matters is that the live databases sit
# in the repository root next to the source. deploy/Dockerfile is careful today
# and copies only package.json, package-lock.json, packages/ and tsconfig*.json,
# so nothing sensitive reaches a layer — but it is one `COPY . .` away from
# baking real account material into an image that is meant to be distributable,
# and that mistake is invisible until somebody pulls the image and unpacks it.
# Excluding the material here means the daemon never receives it in the first
# place, so the careless COPY has nothing to find.

.git
.gitignore

# Dependencies and build output are reproduced inside the image from the
# lockfile and the TypeScript sources. Copying the host's copies in would at
# best waste the transfer and at worst ship native modules compiled against a
# different libc than the runtime stage's.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist

# tsc --build is incremental and decides what to emit from these. If dist/ is
# excluded but the build info is not, tsc concludes inside the container that
# everything is already up to date, emits nothing, and produces an image whose
# entry point does not exist. The two exclusions belong together.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The Android client. Never part of a server image, and by itself the reason the
# context was measured in gigabytes.
android
*.apk
*.aab

# Local scratch scripts and the design canvases: not part of the product.
scratch
design

# The live databases, in the repository root right now, WAL and shared-memory
# files beside them. These hold real registrations and undelivered envelopes.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# Filled-in deployment environment files. The examples are safe and are not
# copied anyway; a real one carries a provider credential.
deploy/**/.env

# Audit and review notes. Internal prose about where the weaknesses are, which
# is not something to hand out inside a shipped image.
SECURITY-AUDIT.md
audit-*.md

# Editor and OS leftovers.
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
